    "url": "https://www.midwest-tropical.com/bubble-wall-kit-how-to-build-a-wall-water-features-indoor/",
    "inLanguage": "en-US",
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://www.midwest-tropical.com/bubble-wall-kit-how-to-build-a-wall-water-features-indoor/",
    "headline": "Create Your Own Indoor Water Feature with Bubble Wall Kit",
    "description": "Create a stunning indoor wall water feature easily for your garden using slate tiles for a beautiful waterfall installation.",
    "articleBody": "\u0026nbsp;  Adding wall water features indoor to a wall in your garden is a simple construction project with outstanding results. Build your waterfall on wall with slate tiles or a solid sheet of hand-painted marble, or Plexiglas rocks. You can find all the supplies for your bubble wall kit at your local landscape fountain or home improvement store.  Wall Water Features Indoor: Instructions   \tDetermine the height and width of the river rock wall.  \tTake measurements for your local landscape supply store, and they will tell you how many rivers, rocks, and mortar you will need to complete the project.  \tThe height of the wall will determine the strength of the pump that you need to purchase. The pond liner is your reservoir and should be at least as wide as the wall.  \tAlternatively, you can buy a plastic sheet sleeve and pool for your wall. This will require additional river rock to be placed around the jacket to keep it immobile.  \tExcavate the ground where the wall will be built. Level the environment as much as possible and remove any grass, rocks, or other debris.  \tMix mortar and apply a thin coat along the length of the wall.  \tPlace the first river stone at one end of the length of the wall.  \tApply mortar to the side of the stone before putting the next rock in place.  \tRepeat this process to build the first row of the rock. Next, begin to build the wall upward, the river rock on top of the mortar joints of the previous row of stacking so that the wall has more stability.  \tLet the mortar dry before moving on to the next step.  \tDig a hole to fit the pond liner in front of the river rock wall.  \tThen, insert the lining into the opening. You don't need preformed liners to be held in place with rocks, as would the plastic sheeting, but you can choose to place river rocks around the front as camouflage.  \tWrap the fountain pump in a nylon stocking to avoid clogging by debris. Secure the pump to a brick with a rubber band to prevent it from moving around in the reservoir. Connect the plastic tubing included with the pump and place the pump in the pool.  \tLay the pipe inconspicuously up to the back of the river rock wall and attach the tip to the top of the wall with a small piece of tape.  \tFill the reservoir with water before starting the pump.  Tips and Warnings:   \tAdd a timer to the pump so that the water source runs automatically  \tElectrical cable burial from reservoir pump to an outlet for safety  How to get rid of dirt in your indoor water wall features  Over months or years, indoor water wall features can accumulate a considerable amount of debris and dirt. If there is enough organic matter at the bottom of the fountain, grass seeds can settle and germinate, creating a layer of grass. Although grass may look unsightly, it is relatively easy to remove with a bit of cleaning.  Instructions:   \tScoop most debris from the waterfall on Wall with gloved hands or a plastic spoon (avoid using metal; it can wear down the surface).  \tRemove the pump from the fountain, if present, following the manufacturer's instructions.  \tFill a bucket with a mild cleanser solution (1 tablespoon of liquid laundry soap per quart of water).  \tScrub the clean source of debris and dirt with a nylon brush or natural bristles.  \tPeriodically wipe off soapy residue and dirt with a cloth or sponge.  \tPay particular attention to cleaning the area where the pump is connected to the fountain tank.  \tWipe the fountain down with a cloth saturated with clean, hot water to remove any soap residue.  Tips and Warnings:   \tRead the source manufacturer's instructions before cleaning. These cleaning instructions are suitable for most sources of most materials. However, if you are cleaning fountain instructions conflict with the instructions above on any point follow the manufacturer's instructions instead.  \tTo avoid another sod problem, keep your fountain running as much as possible and clean every one to three months.  \tIt would be best if you cleaned the inside and outside of the waterfall on wall pump before using the fountain again. Then, follow the manufacturer's instructions for mounting, cleaning, and mounting.",
